      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three practical ways to protect your study time while still seeing them: - **Set a firm time window in advance:** Let them know your availability before the day arrives (e.g., \"I can help set up from 1 to 3, but then I have to leave to study\"). Having a pre-announced end time makes it easier to step away.\n- **Trade open-ended help for one specific task:** Instead of being on call for everything, volunteer for one contained job—like picking up groceries the day before or bringing food—so your time on the day itself isn't completely consumed.\n- **Give an early heads-up about exam season:** Tell them a few days ahead that upcoming tests mean your schedule is booked, so you'll be coming as a guest to visit for a bit, but won't be able to do the prep or cleanup this time. See if any of those fits the way your family usually operates, or if one feels like the easiest to try first.",
